#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124290 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "ccfdc303-534f-530e-810b-f475a997f5d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4703" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1} & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124291 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "22a77802-4114-516f-a0e0-4cda2e069361" :question/math-academy-id "e-4704" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1} & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{5} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124292 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124479 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6e4b2e85-86a8-5050-a60a-ae8d40453ad0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4705" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124293 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "3ac076bd-5add-5c08-bb96-7b11c0a37d54" :question/math-academy-id "e-4706" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b787c6f6-5351-5e11-97e1-60d594c3bcbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574349} {:answer/id #uuid "65255442-2320-5c93-8e6a-cfb6ce46e3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b787c6f6-5351-5e11-97e1-60d594c3bcbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574349} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ed99ac0-e5b7-560b-99f7-88135ed6262b" :answer-field/key "Column 1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53f41b57-4f9f-516e-bd2c-2ecf22bc60cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574351} {:answer/id #uuid "530276a6-e403-5961-9ae6-d6981d600683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53f41b57-4f9f-516e-bd2c-2ecf22bc60cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574351} :answer-field/id #uuid "26384055-28c0-5d19-8fc2-aeccb648af0b" :answer-field/key "Column 2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :