5485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdcc6acf-5383-5b11-9305-2a2d610ba1ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-35730" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $2$ pivots in the $1$st and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200ac6c5-14fa-5556-bb1f-7707ac6c7808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574389} {:answer/id #uuid "7d031a2d-ddfc-5cfd-bd78-5a2695bb5b0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d031a2d-ddfc-5cfd-bd78-5a2695bb5b0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574390} :answer-field/id #uuid "74a073f7-812b-5373-938d-8abe88153699" :answer-field/key "Column 1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574677} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6a167e6-2ac7-5994-a8c4-ac79ab18cd29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574391} {:answer/id #uuid "