answer-field/id #uuid "db2dc6ee-e6a4-5218-8e94-937c8bf87508" :answer-field/key "Column 4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c93d2ae4-7e7b-5500-9b27-fd939892ffa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-35732" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3180301-9a4a-5fa6-a6a5-e0adf4811bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574397} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7e724a-317b-5ad9-9312-30dd25209821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7e724a-317b-5ad9-9312-30dd25209821" :