n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd, $3$rd, $5$th, and $6$th columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124479 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29ff8aac-da11-5008-86a3-01592ba764e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368484} {:answer/id #uuid "9ceaef6f-9c72-5e48-957f-a3b4fb381803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368485} {:answer/id #uuid "5f51609c-de29-58f2-96a9-a374c98ed7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368486} {:answer/id #uuid "9fe13fe4-6d18-59d6-b45c-734844d8bb16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368487} {:answer/id #uuid "30845c4d-bc01-5613-a571-9893