e7595ffb3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130946" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -9 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $4$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -9 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182fb941-8820-5ae9-a73b-d1c5430524f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574279} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f594f0-607c-5d7c-b952-5ae51a37bee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8f594f0-607c-5d7c-b952-5ae51a37bee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574280} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde6ac12-cf7d-5007-9d78-b5aa20affa7e" :answer-field/key "Column 1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b89aaa91-dc2a-578f-a09c-365732bec1f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574281} {:answer/id #uuid "441da38d