:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcd1cb26-1c44-5d74-aa8e-2093ab435f98" :question/math-academy-id "q-130950" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124479 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c25b5ef-b912-5c71-9670-944d65285749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414467} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1a92a6-f6d8-5aa2-9a4c-0f2edb4ce9bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414479} {:answer/id #uuid "e884e7e6-8f56-5bfb-a2ca-b9c4594a1a4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414486} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c840b3-dbab-5742-a2b1-8a2edee0b393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414487} {:answer/id #uuid "fa159688-f836-5d57-8c3c-4060d2af4504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e884e7e6-8f56-5bfb-a2ca-b9c4594a1a4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414486} :answer-field/id #uuid "76643a29-5807-570f-8aa9-f5fb774e145b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b4a741d-30d4-5d2c-9fde-2ae106aac7d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-130961" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "293dfe13-f59f-562c-a0be-1139ae738cb1" :answer/type {:d